Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.63,0:00:05.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Population: eight billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.70,0:00:10.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Now… imagine every one of them, gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.87,0:00:12.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Hour one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.54,0:00:16.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The power plants run on, with no one left to feed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.24,0:00:21.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}One by one… the lights go out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.30,0:00:23.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Hour thirty-six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.51,0:00:28.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Beneath New York, seven hundred and fifty pumps have stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.07,0:00:31.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The subway floods.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.73,0:00:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year twenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.51,0:00:35.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Roots split the asphalt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.49,0:00:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Trees rise through the streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.43,0:00:42.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year three hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.43,0:00:46.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}With no one to paint it, the Eiffel Tower rusts…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.02,0:00:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}and falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.47,0:00:51.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Year five hundred.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.46,0:00:56.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Forests have taken back our cities.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.31,0:01:00.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}But one thing we made will outlast us all…
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.24,0:01:01.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.91,0:01:07.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Still here, thousands of years from now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.18,0:01:12.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}So tell me… would Earth even miss us?
